  "title": "Design Settings » Homepage » Primary & Secondary Hero Content | Brilliant Directories Documentation | BD Support",
  "content": "Design Settings » Homepage » Primary & Secondary Hero Content Link: https://support.brilliantdirectories.com/support/solutions/articles/12000106039 Primary Hero Content These settings control the Main Title Text and Sub-Title Text displayed on the homepage of the website. Visual Guide of the Primary Hero Content 1. Content Area Width This setting controls the width used by the Primary Hero Content on the homepage of the website. 2. Content Alignment This setting controls the location of the message; the options are Left, Right, and Center Left Right Center 3. Font Family This setting controls the Font Family for the entire Primary Hero Content 4. Main Title Text This is the field where to type the Main Title Text for the website 5. Color This setting controls the color of the Main Title Text for the website. 6. Size This setting controls the size of the Main Title Text for the website. 7. Weight This setting controls the weight of the Main Title Text for the website; the options are Light, Normal, Bold, and Extra Bold. 8. Align This setting controls the location of the Main Title Text for the website; the options are Left, Right and Center. 9. Bottom Spacing (padding) This setting controls the amount of empty space added between the Main Title Text and Sub-Title Text. 10. Text Shadow This setting adds a shadow effect behind text to make it stand out or create a stylistic look. 11. Sub-Title Text This is the field where to type the Sub-Title Text for the website 12. Color This setting controls the color of the Sub- Title Text for the website. 13. Size This setting controls the size of the Sub- Title Text for the website. 14. Align This setting controls the location of the Sub- Title Text for the website; the options are Left, Right and Center. 15. Weight This setting controls the weight of the Sub- Title Text for the website; the options are Light, Normal, Bold, and Extra Bold. IMPORTANT NOTE If Primary Content Width is under 100% and aligned left or right, the remaining hero area can be used for Secondary Hero Content to display an image, video, or left blank. Secondary Hero Content (optional) These settings control the Main Title Text and Sub-Title Text displayed on the homepage of the website. Visual Guide of the Primary Hero Content 1. Froala Editor In this section, text, images, or videos can be added to display next to the Primary Hero Content. 2. Mobile View This setting controls whether the content shows on Mobile View or not. Hide on Mobile Show on Mobile For additional assistance: Email support@brilliantdirectories.com or create a ticket Inside Your Account Dashboard . Was this article helpful and accurate? Yes No Send feedback Sorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
